source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons backup create -h <==
Back up WTF/: every live client's, or the clients -t names

Usage: omaddons backup create [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --verify  Hash every file copied, so the backup records its content
      --auto    Make the after-play checkpoint, only when one is due

Examples:
  omaddons backup create                  every live client that has a WTF/
  omaddons backup create -t era --verify  also hash every file copied

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons backup create --help <==
Back up WTF/: every live client's, or the clients -t names

Usage: omaddons backup create [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --verify
          Hash every file copied, so the backup records its content
          
          The backup's integrity is then verified.

      --auto
          Make the after-play checkpoint, only when one is due
          
          Skipped (exit 0, with the reason) when WTF/ is unchanged since the last checkpoint.

Examples:
  omaddons backup create                 every live client that has a WTF/
  omaddons backup create -t retail --reason "before the raid"
  omaddons backup create -t era --verify also hash every file it copied
  omaddons backup create --dry-run       how much it would copy, and the space free
  omaddons backup create --auto -t retail   an automatic checkpoint, only when due

A backup is a copy of WTF/ in Interface/.omaddons/backups/, made without stopping
other changes. On btrfs and xfs it shares its data with WTF/ until either changes.
Stable means WTF/ was observed not to change while it was copied (not a filesystem
snapshot); best effort means it changed even on a second try. --auto follows
auto_backup: it makes none while the game runs, when WTF/ is unchanged since the last
checkpoint, or (with daily) where the filesystem cannot clone files.

See also: backup list, backup verify

Global options:
      --json             One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>  The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run          Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>    Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>    Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running    Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --no-color         No ANSI color
      --no-progress      No progress output
      --progress <MODE>  Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet            Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...       More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help             Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
